web SPA: vite+react19+ts-strict+zustand. every capable browser, capability-gated degradation (src/core/capabilities.ts: chromium/screenCapture/systemAudioCapture/camera/webCodecs/opfs/ios/appleWebKit). Apple WebKit: no tab/system audio; iOS: no screen capture in any browser (native-only, TASKS P5) — UI drops unsupported channels from the effective config; an unusable input renders red (slashed icon), stays clickable, shows its per-platform reason only on press (channels.ts unsupportedReason). NO human-facing doc exists: every file in .ai/ and docs/ is for agents, current truth only.
src/core = framework-free engine; src/app = react UI (imports @core/* only via module indexes). contracts: src/core/types.ts (authoritative) — the seam a native core implements later (DECISIONS 2026-09-02 (3): native at maximum, same contract, shared timeline/edit/sync/governor/report/UI).
code-split (O7): first paint = app shell + capture screen (~219 KB, gate ≤300). editor chunk React.lazy behind app/editorChunk.ts (ONE import() so lazy + prefetch resolve the same chunk), prefetched when recording starts; session.ts/recovery.ts (drag mediabunny) load via core/capture/lazy.ts and are WARMED at mount by warmCapturePipeline(); supabase loads on first cloud use. ENFORCEMENT: the @core/capture barrel never re-exports session/recovery VALUES. Report modules are fetched only AFTER a take ends (S1).
PWA (P2): manifest + public/sw.js, registered in PRODUCTION ONLY; precaches the whole build from /asset-manifest.json (last 3 builds kept) so a tab that spans a deploy still records (B3); same-origin GET assets only; range requests pass through. A tab left open across a deploy runs the OLD bundle (CLAUDE.md: bust the SW before judging).
capture: getDisplayMedia fired FIRST, synchronously inside the record-click gesture (WebKit drops transient activation on any prior await), granted cam/mic overlap the open picker, ungranted run after it; arm() awaits every device then start() activates all at one epoch. displayInflight.ts refuses a second display request per document (a wedged request never settles; the press fails 'stale' and the app refreshes); displayWedge.ts/wedgeJournal.ts = the safe-mode ladder that climbs back (W1); second origin inout-kappa-two = the per-site discriminator (docs/SCREEN_WEDGE.md). RAW VIDEO (X6, default since 2026-08-26): MediaStreamTrackProcessor → frames to rawVideo.worker.ts → hardware VideoEncoder avc (candidates 42E01E…640040, odd sides evened, level ≥5.0 above 1080p, `latencyMode:'quality'`) → fragmented MP4, keyframe every 2 s plus one early key (H2b), own SyncAccessHandle; 1 fps keep-alive when the source is static; MediaRecorder = capability/start-failure fallback (`?rawcodec=mediarecorder`). RAW AUDIO (A1, default since 2026-09-01): `?audiotap=track` reads AudioData off a CLONE of the track via MediaStreamTrackProcessor (no AudioContext, no render deadline — the worklet lost 10 % of a take under CPU load), batched 1024 frames → WebCodecs opus → mediabunny webm; the AudioWorklet tap is the Safari/fallback lane. Anchors (B7): audio = min-filter over batch arrivals minus the platform's reported input latency (10 ms for every device — a Bluetooth headset's real 100-300 ms is invisible); video = performance.now() at frame READ (measuredVideo.ts; a real screen's first frame once arrived 233 ms late); all four anchor inputs persist in ChannelDiagnostics.anchor. Composite origin carried SIGNED (B9). Every channel drains at stop (P0-tail/P0-tail-raw: throttle the source to 1 fps, never end the track); a stop past the 5 s budget keeps what reached disk — demux outranks the wall clock, a locked file is never deleted (H5). A device that dies or never delivers is said and stamped in Recording.lost (H4: composite liveness tick at 5 s → `channel-dead`; raw encoder framesIn===0 at stop); a component death closes the segment and opens the next, 1.5 s cooldown, 4 per channel (H1, segmentContain.ts). setChannelActive(kind, active) releases/re-acquires mid-take as a new segment; pause()/resume() (F6) exist with NO UI (Robert 2026-09-02: wire it — U2). No take-length cap: diskGuard.ts reads the origin's storage growth, prints minutes-left on the idle capture screen (rate = this machine's median), auto-stops when the disk runs out (B5). Encoder budget (O15, ON): every take prints its encoder plan; the budget is EARNED from this machine's own collapses and drops the COMPOSITE first, the screen's size last (since J6 the composite is not encoded anyway, so on the shipped rung there is only the size left to drop). The first VideoEncoder per Chrome process costs ~3.2 s → warmed at mount, the warm yields to a committed take (H6). Recording preview = the editor's stage, WYSIWYG. `?synthetic=1` = generated streams; test knobs in docs/FLAGS.md.
live composite: v2 = liveCompositeV2.ts + compositor.worker.ts (DEFAULT since 2026-08-24; frames transferred to the worker → compositorGL.ts WebGL2, 2D fallback → VideoEncoder avc realtime, keyframes ≤2 s → fMP4 → own SyncAccessHandle; frame-driven, 1 fps keep-alive), v1 = liveComposite.ts (main-thread canvas → MediaRecorder) = capability/start-failure/watchdog fallback (`?engine=v1`). Composite audio stays on the main thread (v1 mix graph tapped by an AudioWorklet that is also the liveness tick; PCM batches carry the AudioContext time of their first sample). Never OPENED at max (max = 2 raw encoders, and that take has no composited preview and no liveness detector either). SINCE J6 (2026-09-04, `?glue=`) IT IS PAINTED AND NEVER ENCODED wherever it is opened: `CompositorStartMsg.record=false` builds no encoder, no muxer, no OPFS handle and no audio mix (the AudioWorklet tap still ticks — it is the liveness clock), `stop()` resolves null, and both engines take the rung. The preview and the frozen-screen detector are downstream of the DRAW and are untouched; a late join and a pause no longer cancel it, because both reasons were about the file. `?glue=record` restores the second encoder and the file. `stopStats.glue` carries P9's intake, O4's painter and the painted-frame count for a take with no CompositeRecording to carry them.
pressure (E1, core/pressure.ts, deliberately outside capture/): four leading signals from the compositor worker (encoder queue depth at submit, encode latency vs the pipeline it can hold, worker scheduling lateness MEAN, sync cost per frame), 4/s, levels nominal/fair/serious/critical, bands read off this machine. The rate ladder steps BEFORE loss (rate only: captureLadder rule 1 — a rung is a RATE, the size never moves), climbs back the tick pressure clears, veto capped by VETO_MAX_MS; `?pressure=0` = the old autopsy ladder. core/backgroundWork.ts brokers every background job on the same reading (full/half/trickle/paused). SINCE J6 THE FOUR SIGNALS COME FROM THE RAW SCREEN CHANNEL'S ENCODER (rawVideo.worker.ts, M1's shared sampler) and are handed to the composite's ladder through `LiveCompositeV2Handle.notePressure`: the composite no longer encodes, so its own worker starts no sampler at all — a reading whose encoder block is unmeasured and whose cpu block is a 0.4 ms draw would call a drowning machine nominal. Max opens no composite at all, and M1 lifts the same instrument into the same worker as max's EMERGENCY floor — never a second implementation. RULING 2026-09-02: bias UP (E2) — history only raises, down only on distance-to-loss, unseen work shed first, bursts absorbed, picture last; background work paced to its deadline, never flat out.
store: OPFS blobs (blobStore + SyncAccessHandle durable worker) + IndexedDB metadata (recordingsRepo, `inout` FROZEN at v2: an old tab blocks any versionchange forever) + the EDIT (editsRepo) + EXPORT JOBS (jobsRepo, own `inout-jobs` DB) + THE PENDING MANIFEST (recovery.ts, own `inout-pending` DB, `durability:'strict'`, ALSO localStorage; salvage reads whichever survived — H2b). Crash bound ~2 s at any length; kills from 2.3 s recover (H2/H2b). Editor saves debounced 400 ms; recovery restores it, falling back to the default edit on any read failure. Media files are re-typed from the recorder's real mimeType (Safari wrote MP4 under .webm — F13 third pass).
timeline: pure math, unit-tested. channel trims blank (no time shift); global trim = output bounds. MID-TAKE CUTS (F1): EditState.segments = ordered kept RECORDING-timeline spans; output→recording maps PIECEWISE (outputToRecordingMs; channelSourceTimeAt built on it). editSegments() = what the editor holds (a split is two adjacent spans); keptSegments() merges adjacent spans (contiguous material is NOT a cut → a split with nothing deleted stays on the instant path). The editor's x() is piecewise: a closed cut takes no width; per-clip speed (F5b, timeStretch.ts WSOLA, 0.5-2×).
camera (F4): timeline/cameraTrack.ts = SINGLE source of truth for the PiP pose at an instant; export compositor and editor stage both sample it (parity by construction). FRACTIONS of the frame (centre + width), height follows the camera aspect; absent = the fixed BR-24 % slot (unit-pinned). A drag writes a PAIR (anchor at T−CAMERA_MOVE_MS, target at T). A track ⇒ isDefaultEdit false ⇒ never the packet copy. Live drag during recording moves the pipPose (UI1). zoom/pan = timeline/viewportTrack.ts (F2/F2b, max 2.5×, a zoom moves as a whole). background frame (F3) = compose/background.ts presets as DATA, painted by the export and by the editor's CSS; inactive style dropped by clampEditState.
geometry + rate (F13/F15/F18 = what `max` MEANS since UI1): a quality step is a PIXEL BUDGET resolved against the take's aspect (src/core/frame.ts → vertical video from a phone; the first delivered frame's aspect is adopted because `getSettings()` describes the sensor), the rate follows the source and only goes UP (src/core/rate.ts, 60 at max, 30 below); `max` = the take's own long edge; nativeres ON = the screen captured at its own size (odd sides evened); `?resstep=1` (OFF) lets the raw channel follow a mid-take size change by segmenting (30 ms step, 69 ms seam, O16). Quality is ONE decision made BEFORE the take (slider, `inout.quality.step`, default 1080p = "high"); the editor's slider only goes DOWN from the recorded step. RULING 2026-09-02: max = paid only.
compose: mediabunny + WebCodecs. THREE EXPORT PATHS chosen by compose/choose.ts in order: INSTANT packet copy (unedited, and SINCE J6 only over the RAW channel — there is no composite file: the step must match the take's geometry, single generation O3b/O3c, one 4:2:0 generation fewer, copy source resolved once in copySource.ts. A take with a CAMERA has nothing to copy and takes the render, pre-made at stop), SMART CUT (pixel-default edits: copy packets, re-encode [cut → next keyframe], avcC byte-compared, v1 composites refused up front), RENDER (compose/render.ts in export.worker.ts, in-thread fallback; 5-6× realtime, decode-bound — X4 refuted threading, X5 GPU compositor refused on parity, O5b pipelining already there). Render: sample channels per frame → canvas layout → encode; mp4 avc+aac, fallback avc+opus, then vp9+opus webm; codec ladder seam av1-hw → hevc-hw → avc floor, above-floor reachable only with allowAboveFloor (SIZE-CODEC: the DESTINATION decides the codec, unknown egress = AVC). Constant quality `?cq=` ON (H.264 quantizer qp20 + governor; bitrateMode is inert in Chrome); export keyframe every 5 s (O11b); PiP camera 2.5 Mbps (O11c); every export backpressured (R2: 14,400 queued frames once killed the GPU process). audio: every path mixes from the RAW channels (Hermite resample to 48 kHz, u/(1+u) soft limit, seam-safe 1 s chunks, ±3 ms fade at every cut join, onset-aware level gates); makeup = p90 bounded by the p20 noise floor and the peak licence (`?loudness=r128` = BS.1770 −14 LUFS, built, a no-op until attenuation is allowed — exports sit 1-9 dB above −14). loudness envelope measured DURING capture (O2/X1, Recording.loudness) so export, Tighten and the editor skip the probe unless a fence says otherwise. silence tightening (F5a): timeline/silence.ts pure envelope → proposals; analyzeSilence measures the SAME envelope as the normalizer. THE RENDER REMEMBERS (J1, `?chunked=`, ON): the output is cut into GOP-aligned chunks at the export keyframe interval in exact output FRAME indices; each chunk is an OPFS file NAMED BY ITS CONTENT (recording + settings + the edit RESTRICTED to that chunk's span, compose/chunkPlan.ts) published by a rename after finalize, so a key that exists means bytes that are complete — which makes the chunk cursor the resume cursor and the shipping cursor (`shippableChunks()`) at once. The export concatenates by PACKET COPY with the avcC byte-compared across chunks; anything it declines falls back to the unbroken render. The AUDIO is one continuous artifact under its own key (priming forbids splicing it), so no picture edit costs any audio work. One reader set per contiguous run of misses; the chunk loop runs INSIDE the export worker. Cache capped at a quarter of the origin's quota, LRU, 24 h. ANY change that moves a pixel must bump chunkPlan.ts's KEY_VERSION. PRERENDER (F16/F16b, narrowed by J3 2026-09-03, widened in effect by J6 2026-09-04 — every camera take's export now renders, so every camera take's stop starts one): compose/prerender.ts renders in the background keyed on recording+edit+settings — AT STOP for any take whose export would render — paced by `?bgpace=` on the pressure broker (first load shed), joined by a later export press, re-keyed by a split, superseded by any other edit; can only SAVE time. THE EDIT-TRIGGERED START IS BACK, ON, AND BEHIND ONE DOOR (J5 2026-09-04, robert (27) reversing robert (23) himself): `core/compose/editRender.ts` is the only thing in the app that may start a render because of an edit, and it enforces four rules — opening a take starts nothing, an undo back to the take as it opened cancels what is pending, a packet copy or a smart cut starts nothing, and a real edit starts ONE job 1.2 s after it settles, on J1's content-keyed chunks so a superseded job loses only the chunk it was inside. `?bgrender=0` is J3's behaviour. Still pinned by src/app/screens/prerenderTrigger.test.ts, which reads the shipped source, because what it guards is still partly an ABSENCE. bits audit (O11a, compose/bits.ts) prices every size lever. certification (O8, compose/certify.ts) = JSON in the container comment tag of every export: path, settings, loudness makeup+source, stalled/missing channels, cut count, CI sync bound, codec rung; anchors deliberately NOT in it. exports STREAM TO DISK (O1: mediabunny StreamTarget → OPFS scratch, ~4 MB held; BufferTarget fallback). EXPORTS ARE BACKGROUND JOBS (compose/exportJobs.ts + jobsRepo): a press snapshots the edit and returns; ExportDock (every screen) shows progress/ETA/cancel then the saved row; parallel; restart from zero after refresh (max 3 — J1 makes them resumable); rows expire 24 h; finished file downloads then is copied to its own `xjob-*` key. Size panel: model + calibration probe (F7c/B1/B1b; sizeConfidence exact/measured/provisional/rough).
report card (S1, core/report/reportCard.ts + takeJournal.ts): twelve dimensions (channels · audio continuity · audio clock · rescue bursts · picture · rate · elastic · sync anchors · storage · memory · lateness · wedges), green/red/incomplete (incomplete is never a pass), computed at stop and on demand: `await __inoutReport()` / `__inoutReportAll()` / `__inoutTakeLog()` (60-entry localStorage ring) / `__inoutEditorReport()` (the editor's own card). Recording.stopStats (heap, storage headroom, requested rate, what was given up, the elastic ledger, the lateness summary). Console only — Robert 2026-09-02: bug data is not shown to users. Playbook docs/TAKE_REPORT.md.
main-thread lateness (G7, core/lateness.ts + latenessBeat.worker.ts): scheduled-vs-actual on the MAIN thread, sampled from the press to the stop and over the editor's first 15 s, graded against Phase 1's own claim (worst one-second window > 30 ms = fail). THE CLOCK IS IN A WORKER and the main thread only stamps arrivals: a take runs with the document hidden and Chrome clamps a hidden page's timers to ~1 Hz — measured 2026-09-02 in one hidden page, `setInterval(16)` read 1.2 Hz / p50 983.6 ms late while the worker beat read 63.3 Hz / p50 0.0 ms. O(1) per take (fixed histogram, worst three windows, exact max); attribution from long-animation-frame / longtask, which report nothing on a hidden document and so name owners in the EDITOR only. `?lateness=0` off, `?latebeat=N` changes the period. Rig scripts/g7-lateness.mjs.
for-AI export (AI1, core/ai, built in ai.worker.ts — X9): one PDF, page 1 = signal-derived text index, then pixel-delta keyframes (cursor filtered by the delta's shape, pointer trail in the index); button in QualityBar; spec docs/AI_EXPORT.md. Known weakness (Robert 2026-09-02): the delta picker dropped frames whose only change was small (cursor, text fields); ~144k tokens per 97 s.
share: saveToFile + ShareTarget list. cloud: supabase adapter behind CloudProvider (google oauth, private bucket, signed URL, quota+ttl); NULL when env unset — prod has no env, so cloud UI is absent today. E2EE-compatible (provider needs no plaintext beyond size/name); RULING 2026-09-02: paid cloud = encrypted, we never see files, no extra user steps; storage with free egress; users' own disks connectable.
auth: GOOGLE ONLY (RU alternatives removed 2026-08-23; "just for now, no limits here" 2026-09-02).
platform + QA (P3): core/platform.ts answers WHICH browser and whether too old (YaBrowser/Edg/OPR matched BEFORE Chrome; on iOS every skin is WebKit); capabilities.ts is the only "can it do X" (engine × OS: Chromium on Windows carries system audio on a monitor share). CHROMIUM_FLOOR=107 = vite's baseline target (raise together); the floor only WORDS a failure a probe found. REQUIRED_FEATURES is main-thread-observable only. window.__inoutSupport = the one verdict. Runners: scripts/browser-check.mjs (prod build, real browser, record→edit→export, 8 gates) · scripts/ru-reachability.mjs · docs/QA_MATRIX.md, docs/RU_REACHABILITY.md.
analytics: event bus, console dev / noop prod — nothing leaves the device today.
UI flow: capture → editor (zustand state machine, AppMode exactly those two). Capture screen = quality slider + input chips (red = unsupported, tap for reason; toggles mid-take) + record + live stage (camera draggable) + disk-minutes + wedge notices + hidden TestPanel (`?test`, flags — Robert 2026-09-02: every flag becomes a product decision or is deleted, U4). Editor = framed stage (zoom drag, camera drag) + transport row (back · continue[F19] · play · time · scrubber · Export · For AI) + tools (split, tighten, speed, frame presets) + lanes with filmstrip/waveform (ruler above) + take library (delete/watch/edit; decoded mid-take frame on the card). Keys: space, ←/→. U1 THE ON-TOP PANEL (shipped 2026-09-02, `?panel=0` off): `documentPictureInPicture` window opened BY the record press and closed with the take — timer, audio ring, Stop, Pause/Continue, making the same session calls the page's own button makes. app/panelChunk.ts owns its one dynamic import (off first paint, warmed at mount, O7); app/lib/recorderPanel.ts owns the window (its own CSS written into an empty document; the browser's 34 px title bar and its origin string are not ours). ORDER INSIDE THE PRESS IS LOAD-BEARING: `requestWindow()` consumes the click's transient activation and `getDisplayMedia` does not, so the screen request is dispatched first and `whenDisplayDispatched()` (displayInflight's pending predicate) holds the panel behind it.
